==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_ShareeInSameTeam  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_ShareeInSameTeam.als
    rationale: Clearing F_ShareeInSameTeam removes the constraint that sharedWith users must be in the same team as the task. The injected violation forces a cross-team user into sharedWith, which both NoInformationLeakage and FR_012_CrossTeamSharingForbidden assert must be impossible.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_006_CrossTeamAbsoluteIsolation, FR_012_CrossTeamSharingForbidden
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_CrossTeamAbsoluteIsolation: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_CrossTeamSharingForbidden: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OwnerOnlyShareControl  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_OwnerOnlyShareControl.als
    rationale: Clearing F_OwnerOnlyShareControl removes the restriction that only task owners may author shared/unshared audit events. The injected violation forces a non-owner actor to author an OpShared entry, which FR_010_OwnerOnlyShareControl and OwnershipBasedAccess must catch.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_010_OwnerOnlyShareControl
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_010_OwnerOnlyShareControl: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries removes the constraint that OpDeleted is terminal and unique. The injected violation forces two distinct OpDeleted entries for the same task, representing a re-written audit record — exactly what AppendOnly is supposed to prevent.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_017_AuditEntriesOutliveTask
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AuditEntriesOutliveTask: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditActorRoleSnapshot  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AuditActorRoleSnapshot.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AuditActorRoleSnapshot allows an audit entry to record a role that does not match the actor's actual role. The injected violation forces a mismatch, which AttributionCorrectness asserts must not occur.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_016_AuditEntryAttribution
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditEntryAttribution: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CrossTeamIsolation  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_CrossTeamIsolation.als
    rationale: Clearing F_CrossTeamIsolation removes the constraint that audit actors must be in the same team as the task. The injected violation forces a cross-team actor to appear in an audit entry, which NoInformationLeakage and FR_006_CrossTeamAbsoluteIsolation both assert is impossible.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_006_CrossTeamAbsoluteIsolation, FR_004_NonShareeCannotAccessTask
      - NoInformationLeakage: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_006_CrossTeamAbsoluteIsolation: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_004_NonShareeCannotAccessTask: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_ShareeCannotDelete  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_ShareeCannotDelete.als
    rationale: Clearing F_ShareeCannotDelete removes the restriction that only owners and admins may author OpDeleted audit events. The injected violation forces a sharee (non-owner, non-admin, in-team member present in sharedWith) to author a deleted event, which FR_011_ShareeCannotDelete must catch.
    expected to FAIL: FR_011_ShareeCannotDelete, LeastPrivilege, OwnershipBasedAccess
      - FR_011_ShareeCannotDelete: FAIL (expected)
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)

